D. Proof interpretation
  The Helly obstruction can be attacked through endpoints, not only measures.
  In this bank every row has a survivor window whose active endpoint spine
  has rank at most 2.  Most best spines are E-only, meaning a whole even-safe
  component already dodges the odd two-color core.  Mixed E/B0 or E/B1 spines
  record the genuine two-color wall cases; the two no-mixed rows are easier
  E-only exceptions, not counterexamples.
  Candidate finite lemma: every primitive covering row has either an E-only
  free component or a mixed even/odd endpoint spine of rank at most 2.

